// Remora-specific module AND installed name. Both halves are forced, and the second one is not
// obvious, so it is written down: a `stem: "binder_alloc"` here is a HARD KATI ERROR in any tree
// that also defines a binder_alloc module —
//   out/soong/installs-remora_x86_64.mk: error: overriding commands for target
//   `out/target/product/remora_x86_64/vendor/bin/binder_alloc', previously defined at ...
// TESTED, not assumed. It is not a matter of what the product installs: soong emits
// install rules for a module regardless of whether the product installs it, so the path collides
// as long as the other project exists in the tree at all.
//
// The installed name therefore moves, and the init.rc line that execs it moves with it, in
// Remora's own container-compat patch for system/core. Those two must change together or the
// image ships an init.rc naming a binary that is not there (bd remora-28ix.4).
cc_binary {
    name: "remora_binder_alloc",
    srcs: ["main.cpp"],
    cflags: ["-Wall", "-Werror"],
    vendor: true,
}
